Map plain Python errors onto the robot's three kinds: OSError / timeouts -> SystemError_ (retry);
ValueError / KeyError (what bad data raises) -> BusinessError BAD_DATA; anything else, TypeError and
AttributeError included (almost always a bug) -> plain RobotError (stop, needs a fix).

Alteryx Filter with several conditions: filter_rows(df, ("ccy", "in", "USD,SGD"), ("amount", ">", 1e6)).
One condition may be given flat: filter_rows(df, "ccy", "in", "USD,SGD"). how='all' (AND) or 'any' (OR);
operators as rules.OPS. Returns (matching, not_matching).

Windows Task Scheduler entry. schedule: MINUTE | HOURLY | DAILY | WEEKLY | MONTHLY | ONCE | ONLOGON;
days='MON,TUE,WED,THU,FRI' (WEEKLY); every=n -> /MO (every 15 with MINUTE). interactive=True (/IT) runs only
while you are logged on (needed for Excel/Outlook COM). dry_run=True prints the command; False creates it.

Flow("recon").step("load", read_sheet, "in.xlsx").step("fx", lambda d: d[d.desk == "FX"]).run()
-> output DataFrame; .trace = DataFrame(step, rows_in, rows_out, cols, ms, status, error);
keep=True stores each step's output in .snapshots.

